format prints

    1. third
    1. fourth

The list started at three and now starts at one. This is not a question of
style: the rendered numbering changes, so a document that referred to "step 3"
in the prose above now points at an item labelled 1.

What it should do: keep the start value the author wrote, and count up from
it.

Cause: BlockFormatter's .list case writes the fixed string "1." for every
ordered item. The start value is never read from the cmark node
(cmark_node_get_list_start) and MarkdownBlock.list has nowhere to put it, so
the information is already gone by the time the formatter runs.

See also format-keeps-an-ordered-list, which is the same line of code on a
list that happens to start at one.
